From fef7ff0d0e467f51a48e6d0944da8c835915d970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cemu-gyro <cemu-gyro@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:00:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: use the built-in Windows IMU as motion source for SDL
 gamepads without sensors

Handhelds like the MSI Claw 8 AI+ expose their gamepad as an XInput device
without motion sensors, while the IMU is a separate Windows sensor
("Physical Gyrometer"/"Physical Accelerometer") that reports through the
custom sensor value fields. SDL can't read those, so the motion option was
greyed out. Poll them with the Windows Sensor API and feed them through the
same integration path as SDL gamepad sensors.
---
